          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Win the most tricks to claim the pot, while ensuring you win at least one trick to avoid the penalty.',
          gameplay: "1. **Ante**: Mandatory contribution. 2. **Deal**: 5 cards each + trump reveal. 3. **Participation**: Players choose to 'Play' or 'Fold'. 4. **Exchange**: Active players may discard and draw new cards from the stock. 5. **Play**: Must follow suit; if void, MUST trump; if trumps are led, MUST over-trump. 6. **Settlement**: Winner takes pot. Non-winners with 0 tricks match the pot.",
          keyRules: [
            "If you choose to Play and win 0 tricks, you are 'Bourréd' and pay the whole pot.",
            'Dealer must play if all other players fold.',
            'Aces are high; 2s are low.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Only stay in the hand if you have at least one high trump or a void in a side suit that allows you to trump early and secure your safety trick.',
          intermediate: "The 'Exchange' Tell: Watch how many cards opponents draw. A player drawing 1 card likely has a strong four-flush or triple; a player drawing 3 is gambling on the draw.",
          advanced: "Defensive Over-trumping: If you hold the second-best trump, wait for the leader to play trumps so you can over-trump and seize control, potentially 'Beasting' (Bourréing) the opponents.",
          tips: [
            "Don't be greedy—avoiding the penalty is more important than winning a small pot.",
            'In a 5-player game, 25 cards are out; use this to estimate if your King-high suit is safe.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
