          deckDescription: 'One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for Bourré (Booray) where the turned card sets trump and players must follow suit or trump.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). The turned card determines the trump suit for the hand; it outranks the other three suits. Follow suit when able; failure to follow or trump when possible may result in a bourré (penalty).',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit: ace high, then king, queen, jack, ten, nine, eight, seven, six, five, four, three, two low. Standard trick order; trump overrides plain suits. The goal is to take at least one trick to avoid paying into the pot.',
